\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The day Thou gavest, Lord, is ended,
\par The darkness falls at Thy behest;
\par To Thee our morning hymns ascended,
\par Thy praise shall sanctify our rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. We thank Thee that Thy Church
\par unsleeping,
\par While earth rolls onward into light,
\par Through all the world her watch
\par is keeping,
\par And rests not now by day or night.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. As o'er each continent and island
\par The dawn leads on another day,
\par The voice of prayer is never silent,
\par Nor dies the strain of praise away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The sun that bids us rest is walking,
\par Our brethren 'neath the western sky,
\par And hour by hour fresh lips are making,
\par Thy wondrous doings heard on high.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. So be it, Lord; Thy throne shall never,
\par Like earth's proud empires, pass away,
\par Thy kingdom stands, and grows for ever,
\par Till all Thy creatures own Thy sway.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

